istics Questionnaire, each with less than 200 words \u2013 Residential only\nAcademic Resume\nB.S. Degree Official Transcript\nGraduate Form 18 \u2013 Required for Concurrent Degree/Certificate Only\nGraduate Record Exam (GRE) \u2013 optional\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\nThe following English proficiency minimum scores are required by this program for the tests listed below by this program (residential only). To view additional English proficiency options accepted by this program and the Office of the Vice Provost for Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Scholars, visit the English Proficiency Requirements page.\nTOEFL: Internet-Based Test (IBT): Minimum Overall Required Score: 80 (For exams taken before January 21, 2026)\nMinimum section requirements:\nReading: 20\nListening: 20\nSpeaking: 20\nWriting: 20\nTOEFL: Internet-Based Test (IBT): Minimum Overall Required Score: 4 (For exams taken on or after January 21, 2026)\nMinimum section requirements:\nReading: 4\nListening: 4.5\nSpeaking: 4\nWriting: 4\nIELTS (Academic Module): Minimum Overall Required Score: 6.5\nMinimum section requirements:\nReading: 6.5\nListening: 6.5\nSpeaking: 6.5\nWriting: 6.5\nThe Online Master\u2019s and Graduate Certificate program follows the minimum English proficiency score requirements established by the Office of the Vice Provost for Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Scholars (OGSPS) for admission.\nGraduate Certificate Program Requirements\nA bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution\nCumulative GPA of 3.0 or equivalent\nAn applicant\u2019s prior education must include the following prerequisites:\nOne (1) semester of Calculus\nIt is recommended that applicants show successful completion of the following undergraduate courses:\nOne (1) semester of Statistics\nKnowledge of Computer Programming\nPrerequisite courses, or equivalent, necessary for admission to the Certificate Program of the Department of Statistics (residential only):\nSTAT 51100\nSTAT 51200\nEquivalency of background courses is determined by the Director of Graduate Programs (graduate@stat.purdue.edu). For substitution approval, please contact the Director of Graduate Programs at graduate@stat.purdue.edu.\nTo earn the graduate certificate in Applied Statistics, a grade of at least B is required for all 4 courses.\nDoctoral and Master\u2019s Degree Program Requirements\nA bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution\nCumulative GPA of 3.0 or equivalent\nAn applicant\u2019s prior education must include the following prerequisites:\nOne (1) semester of Calculus\nIt is recommended that applicants show successful completion of the following undergraduate courses:\nOne (1) semester of Statistics\nKnowledge of Computer Programming\nApplication Deadlines\nResidential\nFall\nSpring\nSummer\nDecember 1\nOctober 1\nNo Entry\nOnline\nFall\nSpring\nSummer\nJuly 15\nDecember 1\nNo Entry\nProgram Contact Information\nResidential\nName: Graduate Coordinator\nPhone: 765-494-5794\nEmail: graduate@stat.purdue.edu\nWeb: Program Website, Statistics \u201cHow to Apply\u201d\nAddress:\nDepartment of Statistics\nPurdue University\n150 North University Street\nWest Lafayette, IN 47907-2066\nUSA\nOnline\nName: Online Program Enrollment Counselor\nPhone: (765) 496-5646\nEmail: POApply@purdue.edu\nWeb: Program Website, Certificate Website\nAddress:\nPurdue Online Admissions\n155 South Grant Street\nYoung Hall, Room 406\nWest Lafayette, IN 47906\nUSA\nAdditional Information\nPlease include information about computer programming skills in the application.\nAn applicant\u2019s mathematical training should include linear algebra and advanced calculus; probability and mathematical statistics are desirable.\nBefore you apply, please visit the Statistics how to apply page.\nFor online programs, please visit the Online Statistics Admissions Requirements and Deadlines webpage.\nNeed help finding something? Contact us \u2014 we\u2019re happy to assist!\nContact OGSPS\nPurdue University\n610 